---
interface Props {
  data: {
    name: string;
    site?: string;
  };
}
const { data } = Astro.props;
const testflight = data.site ?? 'https://testflight.apple.com/join/1RdVtffd';
---

<div class="ps-page ps-display ur-page">
  <nav class="ps-subnav" aria-label="Unroll sections">
    <a href="#top" class="ps-brand" aria-label="Unroll home">
      <strong>Unroll</strong>
    </a>
    <span class="ps-subnav-links">
      <a href="#how">How it works</a>
      <a href="#results">Results</a>
      <a href="#listen">Listen</a>
      <a href="#beta">Beta</a>
    </span>
  </nav>

  <section id="top" class="ps-hero ur-hero" aria-labelledby="unroll-title">
    <div class="ps-hero-copy">
      <p class="ps-eyebrow"><span aria-hidden="true"></span> Private beta &middot; iPhone</p>
      <h1 id="unroll-title">Podcasts, minus the <em>ad breaks.</em></h1>
      <p class="ps-lede">
        Unroll finds the sponsor reads in your podcasts and skips them before you ever hear them.
        Everything happens on your iPhone &mdash; no account, nothing uploaded.
      </p>
      <div class="ps-actions">
        <a class="ps-btn ps-primary" href={testflight} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Join the TestFlight</a>
      </div>
      <p class="ps-release-note">
        Tested on 52 episodes &mdash; nearly 56 hours of real podcasts.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="ur-hero-stats" aria-label="Test results: 95.9% of ads removed, no wrong cuts, none of the show lost, 55.9 hours tested.">
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Ads removed</dt><dd>95.9<small>%</small></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Wrong cuts</dt><dd>0</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Of your show lost</dt><dd>0.0<small>s</small></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Hours tested</dt><dd>55.9<small>h</small></dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="how" class="ps-section ur-detection" aria-labelledby="ur-detection-title">
    <div class="ps-section-head">
      <p class="ps-index">01 / How it works</p>
      <div>
        <h2 id="ur-detection-title">It listens first, <em>so you don't have to.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Unroll checks each episode several different ways before it touches anything, and it only
        skips what it's sure about.
      </p>
    </div>
    <ol class="ur-cascade">
      <li>
        <span>01</span>
        <div>
          <h3>It recognises repeat ads</h3>
          <p>The same sponsor spots turn up episode after episode. Unroll knows them when it hears them.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>02</span>
        <div>
          <h3>It hears where ads are dropped in</h3>
          <p>Ads are usually inserted into an episode. Unroll listens for the telltale pauses and jumps in sound where one begins and ends.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>03</span>
        <div>
          <h3>It follows what's being said</h3>
          <p>Sponsor talk sounds like sponsor talk. Unroll checks the words against what it heard, so both have to agree.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>04</span>
        <div>
          <h3>It only skips when it's sure</h3>
          <p>If there's any doubt, the audio stays in. You might hear the odd ad, but you won't lose part of your show.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="ur-rule">
      <strong>Nothing for you to do.</strong> No reviewing, no approving, no settings to babysit.
      Episodes show up ready to play, and when Unroll isn't confident it simply plays the episode
      untouched.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="results" class="ps-section ur-evidence" aria-labelledby="ur-evidence-title">
    <div class="ps-section-head">
      <p class="ps-index">02 / Results</p>
      <div>
        <h2 id="ur-evidence-title">Tested on <em>real episodes.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Unroll was checked against podcasts where every ad had been marked by hand, then against
        episodes it had never heard before.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="ur-evidence-grid">
      <article>
        <h3>33</h3>
        <p>episodes with every ad marked by hand, so there's no guessing about what Unroll should catch.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>19</h3>
        <p>more episodes used only to make sure it never cuts something that isn't an ad.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>8</h3>
        <p>episodes set aside until Unroll was finished &mdash; a fair test on audio it had never heard.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>52</h3>
        <p>episodes in all, adding up to nearly 56 hours of listening.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="listen" class="ps-section ur-modes" aria-labelledby="ur-modes-title">
    <div class="ps-section-head">
      <p class="ps-index">03 / Listen</p>
      <div>
        <h2 id="ur-modes-title">Keep your podcast app, <em>or use ours.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Two ways to listen. Either way, the ads are handled before you press play.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="ur-mode-grid">
      <article class="ur-mode">
        <p class="ps-index">In your own app</p>
        <h3>Works with the app you already use</h3>
        <p>Unroll gives you an ad-free version of a show's feed. Add it to Overcast, Pocket Casts, Apple Podcasts or Audiobookshelf &mdash; or any app that accepts a custom feed &mdash; and listen as usual.</p>
        <p class="ur-mode-caveat">Still early: for now this works one episode at a time, on the same Wi-Fi as your iPhone. Apps that download through their own servers can't reach it yet.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ur-mode ur-mode-player">
        <p class="ps-index">In the Unroll app</p>
        <h3>A simple player that skips for you</h3>
        <p>Play an episode in Unroll and it jumps over the ads on its own. The original audio is never changed, so if it skips something you wanted to hear, one tap brings it back.</p>
        <p class="ur-mode-caveat">Simple on purpose. It plays, it skips, and it gets out of the way.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="beta" class="ps-section ur-status" aria-labelledby="ur-status-title">
    <div class="ur-status-panel">
      <div>
        <p class="ps-index">04 / Beta</p>
        <h2 id="ur-status-title">Try it <em>before everyone else.</em></h2>
        <p>
          Unroll is in private beta for iPhone, through Apple's TestFlight. Find shows through
          Apple Podcasts or a show's own feed, with nothing extra to sign up for. On iPhones with
          Apple Intelligence, Unroll can also add a short summary and topic list to each episode
          &mdash; again, without anything leaving your phone.
        </p>
        <p>
          It's an early build, so expect a few rough edges.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="ps-actions">
        <a class="ps-btn ps-primary" href={testflight} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Join the TestFlight</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
